 Yes, I can help you with that! Uppy.io is a versatile open-source file uploader for web browsers that supports various plugins for handling different types of file sources. For accessing emails from Outlook or Google, there are two official plugins that might be useful:

1. **Uppy Outlook:** This plugin allows users to attach files from their Outlook mailbox directly to an Uppy upload form. To use this plugin, install it using npm by running `npm install @uppy/outlook` in your project directory. Then, include the plugin in your Uppy instance like this:

```javascript
import UppyOutlook from '@uppy/outlook';

const uploader = Uppy();
uploader.use(UppyOutlook, {});
```

Keep in mind that this plugin requires the user to have an active Outlook session and permissions for the connected account. It also may not support all email clients (e.g., Outlook on the web, Outlook desktop apps).

2. **Uppy Google Drive:** Although not specifically designed for accessing emails, the Google Drive plugin lets users select files from their Google Account storage. This includes emails attached as Google Docs, Slides, Sheets, or PDFs. Install it using npm with `npm install @uppy/google-drive`, then add it to your Uppy instance:

```javascript
import UppyGoogleDrive from '@uppy/google-drive';

const uploader = Uppy();
uploader.use(UppyGoogleDrive, {
  id: 'Google',
  title: 'Google Drive & Google Mail'
});
