 To create a WebSocket server for your chat application using the given database schema in PHP, you can use the Ratchet library by Connective. Ratchet is a WebSocket and Comet library for PHP that's based on the ReactPHP event loop. Here's an example of creating a simple WebSocket server for handling chat rooms:

First, install Ratchet via Composer:

```bash
composer require cboden/ratchet
```

Now, let's create a new file called `index.php` with the following content:

```php
<?php
use Ratchet\MessageComponentInterface;
use Ratchet\ConnectionInterface;
use Ratchet\Server\IoServer;
use Ratchet\WebSocket\WsServer;
use Ratchet\MessageComponentInterface;

require 'vendor/autoload.php';

class Chat implements MessageComponentInterface {
    protected $users = [];

    public function onOpen(ConnectionInterface $conn) {
        $this->users[$conn->sid] = $conn;
        echo "New connection! ({$conn->sid}\n";
    }

    public function onClose(ConnectionInterface $conn) {
        if (isset($this->users[$conn->sid])) {
            unset($this->users[$conn->sid]);
            echo "Connection {$conn->sid} has disconnected!\n";
        }
    }

    public function onError(ConnectionInterface $conn, \Exception $e) {
        echo "An error has occurred: {$e->getMessage()}\n";
        $conn->close();
    }

    public function onMessage(ConnectionInterface $from, $msg) {
        foreach ($this->users as $user => $connection) {
            if ($user !== $from->sid) {
                $connection->send("New message from {$from->sid}: {$msg}");
            }
        }
    }
}

$server = IoServer::factory(
    new WsServer(
        new Chat()
    ),
    8080 // Port number
);

echo "WebSocket server listening on port 8080...";
$server->run();
```

This code sets up a basic WebSocket server using Ratchet.

